# Spark — configuration. Copy to .env and fill in what you need.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored. Never commit a key, and never paste one into a chat.
#
# EVERYTHING RUNS WITH THIS FILE EMPTY. With no provider configured, the
# judgement calls use an explicit deterministic policy, and every number the
# system reports is labelled with the provider that produced it — so a keyless
# run is never presented as a model run.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Provider. One line switches the whole system.
#   deterministic  no model at all (the default when no key is present)
#   groq           free tier — local development and iteration
#   bedrock        the graded evaluation run, so reported token costs are real
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SPARK_LLM_PROVIDER=groq

# Groq: free, no card. https://console.groq.com -> API Keys
# GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...
# SPARK_GROQ_REASONING_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b
# SPARK_GROQ_FAST_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b

# Bedrock: needs `uv sync --extra aws` and AWS credentials in the usual places.
# AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=ap-southeast-1
# SPARK_BEDROCK_REASONING_MODEL=global.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929-v1:0
# SPARK_BEDROCK_FAST_MODEL=global.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pricing, in USD per million tokens. Feeds "token cost per run" and "cost per
# successful connection". Left unset, the report says "unpriced" rather than
# quoting a price that has gone stale — copy the current rates from the
# provider's pricing page rather than trusting a number in a comment.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SPARK_PRICE_REASONING_IN=0.0
# SPARK_PRICE_REASONING_OUT=0.0
# SPARK_PRICE_FAST_IN=0.0
# SPARK_PRICE_FAST_OUT=0.0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Simulation
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SPARK_SIM_PERSONAS=200
# SPARK_SIM_WEEKS=6
# SPARK_SIM_SEED=42

# Upper bound on real model calls in one run. A six-week simulation asks for
# thousands of judgement calls; beyond this budget the rest use the
# deterministic policy, and the report states exactly how many did. Nothing is
# ever dropped silently.
# SPARK_LLM_CALL_BUDGET=200

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Product parameters. The first two are OPEN QUESTIONS, not settled numbers —
# see README "Known limits" and `uv run -m eval.sweeps`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SPARK_REMATCH_COOLDOWN_DAYS=30
# SPARK_MAX_LOCKINS=5
# SPARK_MAX_LOOP_ITERATIONS=5

# Injected voice-bridge failure rate. The bridge is the riskiest call in the
# system; a run in which it never fails has not tested the fallback.
# SPARK_VOICE_FAILURE_RATE=0.02

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Telemetry
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SPARK_TRACE_CONSOLE=0
